OL,3,AFemale DJs call out 'blatant misogyny'
OL,4,Aand harassment in nightlife scene
OL,5,
OL,6,FFemale DJs have described experiencing
OL,7,F"blatant misogyny", harassment and
OL,8,Fintimidation while performing and said
OL,9,Fwomen are often treated as "guests"
OL,10,Frather than professionals behind the
OL,11,Fdecks.
OL,13,FAnna McAteer, Andrea Shearer and Julie
OL,14,FDunne have all spoken about experiences
OL,15,Franging from unwanted interference with
OL,16,Fequipment and inappropriate comments to
OL,17,Fphysical intimidation.
OL,19,FThey said the problem reflects wider
OL,20,Fattitudes towards women working in
OL,21,Fnightlife, rather than being the fault
OL,22,Fof the venues and promoters themselves.
OL,23,APub: 10-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBCultureC Nat RadioFTechnology
